# The ABAP fixtures stand in for real sources and are judged by the bundled
# linter, which reports a CRLF line ending as the abapGit round-trip defect it
# is. A Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true would check them out
# with CRLF and the gate parity test would then fail on `crlf-line-ending`
# rather than on parity - so every checkout gets LF, on every platform.
*.abap text eol=lf

# The vendored agent snapshot code is checked byte for byte against the
# sha256 src/vendor/agent/source.json recorded when it was copied
# (src/test/agentvendor.test.ts). A CRLF checkout would change every hash.
src/vendor/agent/** text eol=lf
src/test/fixtures/agent/** text eol=lf
